Use `git log` with graph formatting:

```bash
git log --all --graph --decorate --oneline --abbrev-commit
```

If you want branches only:

```bash
git log --graph --decorate --oneline --abbrev-commit branch1 branch2
```

For a prettier full repo graph:

```bash
git log --all --graph --decorate --oneline --abbrev-commit --color
```

And if you want a reusable alias:

```bash
git config --global alias.lg "log --all --graph --decorate --oneline --abbrev-commit"
```
